 "sarvam_vocals": {
  "text": "Motion, motion, change in position of an object with time, velocity, acceleration, along a straight line. Coming to everything in the universe, motion, motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run. Sleeping air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries invading every cell. Water flowing down a dam, leaves falling from trees. Rotates once every 24 hours, revolves around the sun once in a year. The sun in motion in the Milky Way, moving with its Local Group of galaxies. Rectilinear motion, uniform acceleration, a set of simple equations, relative nature of motion, relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, size neglected without much error. Motion, motion. Change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line.",
